<overview>
<p>The horse remains the most widely used beast mount in human space, carried to hundreds of worlds during humanity's expansion across the stars. Cavalry traditions stretching back thousands of years on Terra have persisted wherever horses thrive, and many planetary militias maintain mounted infantry formations as a practical and affordable supplement to mechanized forces. Horses are fast, responsive to trained riders, and capable of operating across open terrain, grasslands, and light forest without mechanical support. On worlds where industrial infrastructure is limited or where fuel supplies are unreliable, horse-mounted infantry provide commanders with a mobile reserve that requires only fodder and water. </p><p>Configured for civil disturbance management rather than conventional military combat, these riot control troops are trained in crowd suppression, population control, and non-lethal enforcement operations on garrison worlds during periods of unrest or political transition.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as common date for Sonic Stunner weapon
